    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not say the order on the reals is decidable: max_cases eliminates into Prop, it is a ONE-LEVEL-DOWN fact about Rat, and `forall x y, CReal.le x y or CReal.le y x` is neither proved nor assumed. It does not say `Equiv (abs x) x or Equiv (abs x) (neg x)`: that is a decision on the sign of a real and is not available; everything proved here is one-sided. It does not give max_comm, max_assoc, `max a a = a` as a Rat identity, or `max (a+q) (b+q) = max a b + q` -- nothing consumes them, and each is one more max_cases when something does. It does not introduce Rat.abs: ADR-0512's `-q <= r and r <= q` encoding is still how every bound in the real construction is written, and CReal.abs is `max x (neg x)` one level up. It does not assume or use Markov's principle in any disguise: `not (x ~ 0) -> x # 0` is neither proved nor assumed. And it does not make sqrt, suprema or completeness any cheaper -- abs is the SHAPE those statements take, not a step toward proving them.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
